00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
now turning to the first television  interview with huma abedin hillary  clinton's longtime aide abedin spoke  with cbs evening news anchor and  managing editor nora o'donnell to  discuss her new book both and a life in  many worlds it's published by scribner  an imprint of simon schuster a division  of viacom cbs and on cbs sunday morning  aberdeen discussed her marriage to  disgrace former new york congressman  anthony weiner and how that scandal  affected her job  by 2016 anthony weiner and huma abedin  were officially separated a month after  hillary clinton became the democratic  nominee for president yet another  bombshell  this picture of weiner in bed with their  young son was leaked that triggered an  investigation by child protective  services they're showing up at your  apartment all the time checking on the  well-being of your son were you worried  you would lose your son yes ask any  parent what it feels like  that somebody is judging whether you're  a fit parent and whether you can keep  your child it's hard to put in words a  few weeks later abedine's two lives  truly came crashing together  weiner was caught sexting with an  underage girl and fbi agents found  emails involving hillary clinton on his  laptop  just 11 days before the election fbi  director james comey announced he was  reopening an investigation into  clinton's emails he would finally close  the probe two days before election day  but many considered the damage had been  done  you're right this man weiner was going  to ruin me and now he was going to  jeopardize hillary clinton's chances of  winning the presidency and then you  write you called anthony weiner and you  said what anthony i said wanting to  shake him through the phone  if she loses this election it will be  because of you and me  that night i wrote one line in my  notebook i do not know how i am going to  survive this help me god  yeah  i've just received a call  from secretary clinton it all ended of  course with hillary clinton losing to  donald trump  the debate over what caused her defeat  however has never ended hillary clinton  could be in her second term as president  right now  that is a thought that crosses my mind  probably more than it crosses hers that  is something that lives here  that  i think i'm going to take to my grave  when you say take it to your grave do  you mean because you think about  something you could have done to help  fix the situation make it better because  you're kind of in that fix-it role i  have reconciled and it took me a while  to reconcile that it was not all my  fault i lived with that i did i don't  believe that anymore it's more a sense  of  an ache in the heart  nora o'donnell is joining us right now  good morning so norah this is a very  honest and revealing interview is this  just about her promoting the book or is  it deeper than that  i do think it's deeper than that i think  huma abedin is someone who has been a  private person  largely for the past 25 years as a  hillary clinton aide more public of  course when her husband ran  for mayor of new york but i told i asked  her i said this is your first television  interview this woman has never done a  television interview until our piece on  sunday morning and she said she did it  because she said she realized that if  you don't tell your story someone else  is writing your history it is one of the  most powerful interviews i have ever  done the book is actually one of the  best books i've ever read i'm not in the  business of of  pushing someone's book but she is a  fascinating person that i've known you  know someone who was with hillary  clinton i'm a reporter but i didn't know  her personally she starts off the book  talking about her parents her mother  from pakistan her father from india both  fulbright scholars growing up in saudi  arabia really never ever having a  boyfriend until anthony weiner is really  the only man she's been with and then of  course living her life in this very  public scandal and that giant question  mark which we talk about in this  interview did her relationship with  anthony weiner and those discovered  emails on his laptop somehow lead to  hillary clinton's defeat it's utterly  fascinating it is still an ongoing  question that many people still debate  to this day but norah listen i thought  it was extremely powerful but i thought  she was good but i thought you were  stellar i think it's very difficult to  talk to someone about something that's  so painful so public and so personal and  she did that you both really went all  the way there i think many people  thought that hillary clinton would act  over here patty okay patty's arm's about  to come off  i'll look like daddy too  yeah  many people thought that hillary clinton  and puma that their their relationship  would be fractured after that  um and i think people still are  surprised that it wasn't why do you  think that the two of them are still  extremely close even today  you know it's so interesting uh hillary  clinton has described huma abedine as  her second daughter  and  and huma said to me that everything in  their relationship has been about whom  is well-being first and then their  professional relationship they're  extremely close  and to this day huma abedin is her chief  of staff so she's been working for her  for 25 years however i did ask her  what's next and she kept talking about a  reawakening a rebirth i wonder whether  there is something different in the  future for huma abedin whether it's a  different role or a job where it's a  life in public service as a political  candidate herself i think those are all  potential options in the future uh for  huma abedin  laura we have to go so please answer  this very quickly sure women everywhere  want to know and by women i mean me how  she continued to stay with him time  after time especially when you revealed  yesterday that he was also having sex  with women in their home yes  i think right after this big cycle cycle  of betrayal over and over again i think  yeah it has to do with her son you have  to remember that she was 12 weeks  pregnant when the first public betrayal  happened with the pictures she talks  about a financial decision between the  two of them caring for their son and  then there's more on that but um they  are currently separated and finalizing  their divorce  all right cheering for huma thank you no  doubt and great stuff as usual norah  yeah thank you so much

